{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ag, sorry, this computer is crawling. One second. Right, what's brought you in?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja, um, it's my waterworks, doctor. It burns when I wee.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Burns when you pass urine. How long has that been going?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Four days. Since Monday I think. I don't know, doctor, maybe four days.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, say that again, the screen jumped. Four days?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja. Four days.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): Just the burning, or are you going more often as well?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Much more often, like every hour. And at night I'm up two or three times to wee.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any ache in the back?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja, my lower back is sore, both sides, the bottom bit. Not terrible, maybe a four out of ten. I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Hang on, password again. The burning, the loo trips, and the back, all for those four days?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja. All of it, about four days.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any discharge, anything coming out of the penis?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No discharge. Nothing like that.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Fever? Have you felt hot or shivery?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No. I don't think so. No fever.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): Nausea? Have you been sick?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm, I suppose. Sometimes, not really. I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, was that a yes to the nausea?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really. I can't say. Maybe a bit off once. I don't know.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): I won't mark that as a yes. Travelled recently, coast or overseas?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No. I've been in Joburg the whole time, panel beating out in Germiston. No travel.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any allergy to medicines, penicillin or so?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Nothing I know of.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): What medicines are you on now?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Just panado from the chemist. Two tablets when the back is sore.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Two tablets by mouth? How often?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja, by mouth. When it aches. Yesterday maybe three times, I don't know, doctor, I don't count them.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): Anything else, blood pressure tablets, chronic stuff? Say it clearly, the cursor slipped.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Nothing else. No other medicines.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): Temp on the screen is 37.6. You were sure there was no fever?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Well actually, last night I was proper hot. My wife took it and it was 37.8, and I sweated through the sheet. So ja, a mild fever. I was wrong when I said no.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mild fever then. Any cough, chest pain, shortness of breath? The rest of the chest?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Chest is fine. No cough, nothing sore in the chest.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll feel your tummy. Abdomen is soft, tender low down, lower back tender on pressing. No guarding.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Eina. Ja, that's the sore spot.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): I think this is a urine infection, most likely the bladder, but with the back pain and the temperature I can't exclude the kidney being involved.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): The kidney, is that bad? I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): Often it settles with the right treatment. We'll send urine to the lab today. Sister takes a midstream in the sterile bottle before you leave, and you wait until she says to start.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): Before I go. Ok, I can do that.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (DOCTOR): Bloods Thursday morning at eight, with Sister Nkosi. Come fasting, nothing to eat from midnight, water is fine. Full blood count and a CRP.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): Thursday eight, fasting, from the workshop. Ja.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): If those bloods are borderline, we add a kidney function test, the third one. Only if they're borderline.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): Only if they're borderline. I get it.",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (DOCTOR): No antibiotic today. If the urine grows a bug I'll send ciprobay to the chemist, ciprofloksasin 500 milligrams twice a day for five days. Take it only if I phone and say it's positive.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): Ciprobay, only if you phone. I don't know that one, but ok.",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (DOCTOR): If the burning and the backache haven't settled in a week, we'll book a kidney ultrasound. I'm not booking it now.",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (PATIENT): So the scan is only if it's still there. Do I come back anyway?",
  "[SEG0049] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll see you in this room in one week, Wednesday morning. That's already booked.",
  "[SEG0050] person_2 (PATIENT): Ok. And if I get worse before Wednesday?",
  "[SEG0051] person_1 (DOCTOR): If you get a high fever, you can't pass urine, or you start vomiting, go to casualties, don't wait for me. And drink water, not just coffee."
 ],
